---
const movingTargetBody = [
  'Hi Susan,',
  '',
  "I'd like to book Moving Target for my team.",
  '',
  'Company:',
  'Number of teams (1 to 3):',
  'Rough dates:',
  'In person or remote:',
  '',
].join('\n');

const movingTargetHref = `mailto:hello@susanbrander.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent(
  'Booking Moving Target'
)}&body=${encodeURIComponent(movingTargetBody)}`;

import { talks } from '../data/speaking';

const adaconf = talks.find((talk) => talk.conference === 'ADAConf 2026');
const adaconfSiteUrl = 'https://adaconf.org/';

const bossQuotes = [
  'When priorities change, we either scrap the plan or cling to it.',
  'Nobody feels safe committing without certainty, so decisions get escalated, deferred, or made by default.',
  'Nobody can explain why we built it this way, including us six months later.',
];
---

<section id="work-with-me" aria-label="Work with Susan" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t" style="border-color: var(--color-border)">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[680px] px-6 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold mb-7">Work with me</h2>

    <article id="moving-target" aria-labelledby="moving-target-heading">
      <h3 id="moving-target-heading" class="font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
        Moving Target
      </h3>

      <div class="space-y-5 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          A four hour strategy simulation for engineering, product and architecture teams. You'll
          never have all the information. Moving Target teaches your team to decide well anyway.
        </p>
        {adaconf && (
          <p>
            I ran a two hour version, <a href="#speaking">{adaconf.title}</a>, at
            <a href={adaconfSiteUrl}>ADAConf 2026</a> in November.
          </p>
        )}
        <img
          src="/images/adaconf-2026-workshop.jpeg"
          alt="Susan Brander presenting at the front of a room at ADAConf 2026 while teams at round tables work through the Pets'R'Us scenario paperwork"
          width="1024"
          height="768"
          class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figure class="pl-5 border-l-2" style="border-color: var(--color-accent)">
          <blockquote class="italic">
            "Being a person who has only really worked in technical teams, I really enjoyed the insight
            into all the different parts of the business that need to be taken into account when
            developing a strategy."
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink-muted)">
            Workshop participant, ADAConf 2026
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          Your team becomes the new technical leadership of a fictitious company, with a bold goal
          from the board. They build a strategy, and then things change while they're still building
          it. They leave with the pause: stopping before picking up a task or a request to ask what it
          enables and what it prevents, plus <a href="/pause">a playbook of questions</a> to use on Monday.
        </p>
        <div>
          <p class="mb-3">It's built for teams where you hear:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 border-l-2" style="border-color: var(--color-accent)">
            {bossQuotes.map((quote) => <li class="italic">"{quote}"</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>In person or remote, one to three teams, from $950 ex GST.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href={movingTargetHref}
          class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium text-sm no-underline hover:no-underline transition-colors"
        >
          Book your team
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <h3 class="font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold mt-12 mb-4">Fractional and advisory</h3>

    <div class="space-y-5 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Alongside Kaleida, I take on a small number of fractional and advisory clients. The main way
        in is <strong>The Technical Sounding Board</strong>: a monthly retainer where founders and
        engineering leaders get a senior technical and leadership partner to think through the hard
        calls with, without a full-time hire.
      </p>
      <p>
        I know what this is worth because I've been on the buying side of it. When Kaleida's data
        model stopped flexing and half the team wanted to swap the database, what changed the shape
        of that decision was bringing in someone from outside the team to look at what we'd built
        and what we actually wanted. I've written that one up:
        <a href="/speaking/adaconf-2025-data-pivot">Changing the engine mid-flight</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also always up for turning good work into a good story. If you've got a hard problem
        worth digging into, let's build a case study together: real work on a real challenge, written
        up and shared on stage and in writing, with your blessing.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Either way, start with a conversation.</strong> Forty-five minutes, no charge, no
        obligation. Tell me what you're wrestling with and I'll tell you honestly whether I'm the
        right person for it. If I'm not, I'll usually know someone who is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3" role="list">
      <a
        href="mailto:hello@susanbrander.com?subject=Fractional%20%2F%20advisory%20enquiry"
        role="listitem"
        class="btn-secondary inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium text-sm no-underline hover:no-underline border transition-colors"
      >
        Start a conversation
      </a>
      <a
        href="mailto:hello@susanbrander.com?subject=Building%20a%20case%20study%20together"
        role="listitem"
        class="btn-secondary inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium text-sm no-underline hover:no-underline border transition-colors"
      >
        Build a case study together
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .btn-primary {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
  .btn-secondary {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    border-color: var(--color-border);
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
